# Menu combo while a save dump is in progress, with the game writing BSRAM
# continuously (churn): the dump, the pad frames, the overlay and the pause
# bit must all get through each other on the real serial link -- and the
# game's BSRAM writes contend with the dump's reads on the core's single
# BSRAM port (SNES first, save bytes slip in between).
expect-screen "TangCore"
press down
press b
expect-screen "game.smc"
press down
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-core snestang
wram-burst 0x000 512 0x5A
churn on
poke-save 0x10 0x42
wait-dump
hold select+start+l 500ms
expect-screen "Resume"
expect-config-bit 17 1
churn off
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-config-bit 17 0
